<title>GERMANY: Bertelsmann says EU would block Murdoch.</title>
<headline>Bertelsmann says EU would block Murdoch.</headline>
<dateline>GUETERSLOH, Germany 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bertelsmann AG said it has received notification from cartel authorities in Brussels and Berlin that they would block any involvement by Rupert Murdoch in German pay-TV broadcaster Premiere.</p>
<p>British satellite pay-TV broadcaster BSkyB, in which Murdoch's News Corp owns 40 percent, has been promised a 25 percent stake in Premiere as part of Murdoch's alliance with Bavarian media mogul Leo Kirch.</p>
<p>&quot;We already have a letter from the cartel office that they would block this,&quot; Bertelsmann board member Thomas Middelhoff told reporters.</p>
<p>Middelhoff said BSkyB's involvement with Kirch's DF1 is thus thrown into question.</p>
</text>
